  "verbalization": "Morolic Acid is implicated in the interaction with the Interferon alpha/beta receptor (IFNAR) through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Morolic Acid acts as a target for Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which in turn is targeted by a complex chemical structure, (3R,4S,6S)-10,13-dihydroxy-3-methoxy-6-methyl-5-oxapentacyclo[9.7.0.02,8.04,6.012,17]octadeca-1,8,10,12(17),13,15-hexaene-7,18-dione. This chemical compound is directly linked to IFNAR, indicating a potential mechanism by which Morolic Acid influences the receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Morolic Acid in modulating signaling through the IFNAR, possibly by acting as a ligand or modulator of the receptor. The evidence supports a direct or indirect interaction between Morolic Acid and IFNAR, mediated through the described chemical targets.",
